    description: "Found by the 2026-11-07 docstring staleness audit (dev 4f2feb451b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11072026/review, verify and blind). Corpus impact not measured. cli.py:7836-7838 adds seed.handler to parameter_represented; for a marker entry the request_ingress symbol is the marker (seed.represents), and unseeded_ingress_handlers filters on the entry's own id (verify_claims.py:1080). represented_ingress_callers adds seed.represents (taint.py:4718) but production does not pass parameter_seeds= to it (cli.py:7827). One main.go with save(w, r) writing r.URL.Query().Get(\"p\") plus http.HandleFunc(\"/save\", save): untrusted-input-no-host-fs is VIOLATED through net/http.r, yet untrusted-input-no-subprocess says 'ALSO: 1 request handler(s) receive network data that no taint source represents (ANY /save ...)'. Contradicts the WI-sosov closure note. Cautious-side only. v03 (new)."  # 5fff
